<title>FRANCE: EU grants free-mkt wheat, barley, oats, intvn rye.</title>
<headline>EU grants free-mkt wheat, barley, oats, intvn rye.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following rebates to export free-market grain to non-EU countries, member-country officials said.</p>
<p>			 Tonnage		Maximum rebate</p>
<p> Soft wheat	  343,100		14.90 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Barley		172,500		28.99 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Rye		     1,000		31.45 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Oats		   42,000		34.90 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>The EU also sold 5,201 tonnes of German intervention rye for export to non-EU countries at a minimum price of 103.43 Ecus per tonne, member country officials said. --Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
